{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q421020","formula":"Cu₄Al₂SO₄(OH)₁₂·2H₂O","hill":"Al2Cu4H16O18S","elements":["H","O","Al","S","Cu"],"composition":{"H":16.0,"O":18.0,"S":1.0,"Al":2.0,"Cu":4.0},"names":{"en":"Cyanotrichite","ru":"Цианотрихит","uk":"Ціанотрихіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cyanotrichite is a hydrous copper aluminium sulfate mineral with formula Cu4Al2[(OH)12|SO4]·2H2O, also known as lettsomite. Cyanotrichite forms velvety radial acicular crystal aggregates of extremely fine fibers. It crystallizes in the monoclinic system and forms translucent bright blue acicular crystal clusters or drusey coatings.","ru":"Цианотрихит (Cyanotrichite) — редкий минерал вторичных пластов медных месторождений, находящийся в зонах окисления вместе с малахитом, азуритом и брошантитом. В природе встречается в виде игольчатых кристаллов голубовато-белого оттенка. Впервые был обнаружен в образцах, взятых в районе Молдова-Ноуэ Абраамом Готлобом Вернером в 1808 году.","uk":"Ціанотрихіт (від грец. κύανος або лат. cyaneus — «синій», та грец."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421020","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyanotrichite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A6%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A6%D1%96%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%85%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cyanotrichite-Malac